    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Mexican forces established Fort Lipantitlán in the area in 1831 as a picket fort to deter Anglo-American immigration.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sandy_hollow_escondidas_texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Texian forces captured Fort Lipantitlán in November 1835, contributing to the events leading to the Texas Revolution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sandy_hollow_escondidas_texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early settlement in Sandy Hollow-Escondidas was influenced by Spanish land grants issued to interconnected ranching families in the late 18th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sandy_hollow_escondidas_texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Railroads arrived in the 1880s, connecting Corpus Christi to Laredo and San Antonio to support local agrarian pursuits.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
